{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>He found him in a desert land.</b> It appears to me that the reason it said 'in a desert land' (בארץ מדבר) and did not say 'in the desert' (במדבר) is that the Glory began to enter with them at Etham, which is at the edge of the desert — and this is the meaning of 'in a desert land': in the land adjacent to the desert. <b>So too</b> you find in the section ויהי בשלח (Exodus 13:20–21): ״ויסעו מסכות ויחנו באיתם בקצה המדבר וה' הולך לפניהם יומם״. And the expression ימצאהו embraces two senses: the sense of 'finding' and the sense of 'provision,' according to the Targum — meaning that the Glory found them in the desert land and provided their needs." "<b>And in the waste, a howling wilderness.</b> That is to say: when they departed from settled land and came to a place of waste, a howling wilderness, the grace was completed for them through His bringing them out of Egypt." "<b>He encompassed him.</b> He surrounded them with the clouds of Glory. And according to the Targum, which said אשרינון סחור סחור לשכנתיה, this comes to explain that Israel were at Sinai like a round dance (מחול) and the Glory was among them — and this is what is written (Song of Songs 7:1): ״כמחולת המחנים״ — that round dance of two camps: the camp of Israel and the camp of the ministering angels who descended there with them. And this is like the matter the Rabbis, of blessed memory, said: the Holy One, blessed be He, is destined to make a round dance for the righteous in the Garden of Eden, and His Glory among them. And He said <b>He instructed him</b>, in Torah; <b>He guarded him</b>, that He protected them from Amalek who came to do battle with them and from the other nations; <b>as the apple of His eye</b> — the pupil of the eye is called אישון because it contains the form of a man, and the expression אישון is on account of the smallness of the form; and likewise (Leviticus 16:31) ״שבת שבתון״ — for שבת is said of the essence of the day and שבתון of the addition, and it is an expression of diminution; and likewise the name Amnon (2 Samuel 13:15) — האמינון."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:53:09.178764922Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}